---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Story from '../components/napkin/Story.astro';
import AppShell from '../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/base';
import { library } from '../lib/content';

const { cards, tracks } = await library();
const playgrounds = cards.filter((c) => c.data.griddle).length;
const quizzes = cards.reduce((n, c) => n + c.data.quiz.length, 0);
const flashcards = cards.reduce((n, c) => n + c.data.flashcards.length, 0);

const story = [
  {
    title: 'It started with breaking things',
    text: 'I began my career as a tester who could also write code. Testing teaches you one habit for life: never accept "it just works". Every bug I found started with the same question — why does this actually behave like that?',
  },
  {
    title: 'C++, where every retry is real money',
    text: 'Then I learned C++ to work on payment gateways. In payments a timeout, a duplicate request or a rounding slip is somebody’s money, so you learn to respect the details: idempotency, retries, failure paths, the boring edge cases that decide everything.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Python, and the joy of simple',
    text: 'Next came Python, and I genuinely enjoyed how simple it felt — the code read almost like the idea itself. That stuck with me: when an explanation is right, it should feel that simple too.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Data science and system design',
    text: 'I went on to learn data science and high-level design. Both are full of folklore: rules repeated until they sound like laws, giant diagrams that explain nothing, interview “tricks” with no reasoning behind them. What finally made things click for me was always a small picture and a worked example.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Deep into AI',
    text: 'Then I went deep into AI, and today I work as a Senior Software Engineer specialising in AI. The more advanced the topic, the more I noticed that the hard part is rarely the maths — it is the missing mental picture.',
  },
  {
    title: 'So I drew Napkin',
    text: 'Napkin is the notebook I wish I had at every step: each idea drawn one stroke at a time, explained in plain words, checked against the facts, and then practised until it sticks. I built it with the same tools it teaches — and I use it myself.',
  },
];
---

<AppShell title="Why Napkin" active="about" description="The story behind Napkin — from tester to C++ payments to Python, data science, system design and AI.">
  <div class="container about">
    <header class="about__hero">
      <p class="about__kicker hand">the story behind the napkin</p>
      <h1>Every hard idea I understood, I understood the moment someone <span class="hl">drew it</span>.</h1>
      <p class="about__lede">
        Engineers have always explained the important stuff on whatever paper was nearby — a whiteboard, a notebook, the
        back of a napkin at lunch. Napkin is that habit turned into an app. Here is how it came to be.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div id="journey" class="about__story">
      <Story slug="about" diagram="journey" title="the road to Napkin" tldr="From tester to C++ payments, Python, data science, system design and AI — and why that path led to Napkin." story={story} trackRead={false} after="beliefs" />
    </div>

    <ol class="road" aria-label="The road so far">
      {
        [
          ['Tester', 'never accept “it just works”'],
          ['C++ · payments', 'every edge case is money'],
          ['Python', 'simple reads like the idea'],
          ['DS + HLD', 'pictures beat folklore'],
          ['AI · Sr. engineer', 'the hard part is the mental model'],
          ['Napkin', 'all of it, drawn simply'],
        ].map(([stop, lesson], i) => (
          <li class="road__stop" style={`--d:${i}`}>
            <span class="road__n mono">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <b>{stop}</b>
            <span>{lesson}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <section id="beliefs" class="beliefs" aria-labelledby="beliefs-h">
      <p class="eyebrow">What Napkin believes</p>
      <h2 id="beliefs-h">Simple, not simplistic. Facts, not folklore.</h2>
      <div class="beliefs__grid">
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="pen" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Draw it, don’t describe it</h3>
          <p>Every napkin starts with a picture that builds up scene by scene, so you watch the idea form instead of decoding a wall of text.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="check" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>No superstition</h3>
          <p>Claims are checked, numbers are computed, every runnable Python example is executed on each build and prints the numbers in its worked example, and every napkin cites its sources.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="code" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Ideas first, any language</h3>
          <p>The explanations are language-agnostic: plain words, diagrams and pseudocode. Python appears only in “Implement it” — because it reads like the idea.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="layers" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Learn it once, keep it</h3>
          <p>A quiz checks you actually understood; spaced-repetition flashcards bring each idea back right before you would forget it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="wifiOff" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Yours, and offline</h3>
          <p>No account, no ads, no tracking. Everything works on a plane, and your progress never leaves your device.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="sparkles" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Built with what it teaches</h3>
          <p>The diagrams are code, the flashcards run on FSRS — a modern, research-backed spaced-repetition algorithm — and the whole thing is open source.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="numbers" aria-label="Napkin in numbers">
      <div><b class="mono">{cards.length}</b><span>napkins</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{tracks.length}</b><span>tracks</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{playgrounds}</b><span>playgrounds</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{quizzes}</b><span>quiz questions</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{flashcards}</b><span>flashcards</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="signoff card" aria-labelledby="signoff-h">
      <h2 id="signoff-h" class="hand">A note from me</h2>
      <p>
        If you are preparing for an interview, switching fields, or just tired of explanations that make simple things sound
        hard — I built this for you, and for the version of me who needed it at each of those stops. Start anywhere. Follow
        the drawing. Check the numbers. Then come back tomorrow and see how much stuck.
      </p>
      <p class="signoff__name">— Rahul Tarigoppula<span>Senior Software Engineer, AI</span></p>
      <div class="signoff__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href={href('library/')}><Icon name="library" /> Open the library</a>
        <a class="btn btn--lg" href="https://github.com/RahulTarigoppula/self-learn-napkin" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="external" /> Source on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</AppShell>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .about__hero {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .about__kicker {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    transform: rotate(-1.2deg);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .about__hero h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.4vw, 3.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .hl {
    background: linear-gradient(transparent 58%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--hl) 80%, transparent) 58%);
  }
  .about__lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.22rem);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .road {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr));
  }
  .road__stop {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .road__stop:last-child {
    border-style: solid;
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .road__stop b {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .road__stop span:last-child {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .road__n {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .beliefs {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--topbar-h) + var(--safe-top) + 16px);
  }
  .beliefs h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .beliefs__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  }
  .belief {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .belief__icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .belief h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .belief p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .numbers {
    margin-top: var(--space-9);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .numbers div {
    display: grid;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .numbers b {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .numbers span {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .signoff {
    margin-top: var(--space-9);
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-6);
    max-width: 820px;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background:
      radial-gradient(90% 120% at 100% 0%, var(--accent-soft), transparent 60%),
      var(--paper);
    transform: rotate(-0.4deg);
  }
  .signoff h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .signoff p {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .signoff__name {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: 1.4rem !important;
    display: grid;
  }
  .signoff__name span {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .signoff__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
